WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Species have always gone extinct.

2
00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.080
It's part of life's long history.

3
00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:10.420
Fossils even suggest more species are
alive today than at any time in the past.

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:16.230
Yet in 2019, a global assessment estimated
that about 1 million animal and plant

5
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.510
species face extinction.

6
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.250
So if species have always gone extinct, why
are biologists so alarmed by the extinctions

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.750
happening now?

8
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.320
In this mission, you'll trace
what is driving today's losses,

9
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.470
on land and at sea.

10
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.130
Then you'll read real data on
how many species are threatened,

11
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.850
group by group.

12
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.520
Your mission: explain why today's
extinctions alarm biologists.
